WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.040
Umbral.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.852
From signals to decisions.

00:00:02.942 --> 00:00:05.025
An editorial agenda with evidence.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.813
The agenda ranks five topics for Panama.

00:00:09.903 --> 00:00:14.510
Relevance, impact, urgency, novelty and evidence explain each score.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.798
Filters help you compare the signals.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.706
A topic can have high priority and insufficient evidence.

00:00:22.796 --> 00:00:27.629
Its case sheet shows headlines, provenance, dates and open questions.

00:00:27.719 --> 00:00:30.637
Repetition does not create an independent source.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.662
The assistant searches the same snapshot.

00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:39.361
Ask what still needs checking, then follow the citations back to the evidence.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.762
Prepare a referenced draft from a case sheet.

00:00:44.852 --> 00:00:48.803
This demonstration works offline with a clearly identified template.

00:00:48.893 --> 00:00:51.095
You can edit the text before reviewing it.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:59.208
Record the reviewer and decision, preserve the history and export the case to Markdown.

00:00:59.298 --> 00:01:01.819
Approving a draft does not publish a story.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.927
Sources shows the snapshot, its provisional status and the limits of the data.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.095
Umbral organizes attention.

00:01:13.185 --> 00:01:15.012
Your team keeps the final word.
